# Environment configuration for the scheduled runner.
#
# Copy to .env alongside this file (which is gitignored) and populate.
# Every variable is optional at runtime - the scheduled runner soft-fails
# missing configuration (see src/scheduled-run.ts). That means you can run
# `npm run scheduled` from a dev machine with an empty .env and it will do
# local work only: no notifications, no healthcheck ping, no git push.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ntfy - update and error notifications on your phone
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# 1. Install the ntfy app on your phone (App Store / Play Store / F-Droid).
# 2. Pick a long, random topic name (treat as effectively a secret - anyone
#    who knows the topic can read and post to it).
#    e.g. `openssl rand -hex 16`  -> a6d3f1c2e4b58790a1b2c3d4e5f67890
# 3. Subscribe to that topic in the app.
# 4. Set the URL below, using the full topic URL:
#
# NTFY_TOPIC_URL=https://ntfy.sh/a6d3f1c2e4b58790a1b2c3d4e5f67890
#
# If unset, notifications are logged locally and skipped. See the scheduled-run
# docstring for the notification escalation model (LOW/DEFAULT/HIGH per
# consecutive failures, HIGH on recovery, HIGH on new publication).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Healthchecks.io - dead-man's-switch alert if the runner itself stops running
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# 1. Sign up at https://healthchecks.io (free tier: 20 checks; we need one).
# 2. Create a new check. Set expected period ~1 day, grace ~3h. Add whatever
#    integration you want notifications on (email, ntfy, whatever).
# 3. Copy the ping URL (looks like https://hc-ping.com/{uuid}) below.
#
# HEALTHCHECKS_PING_URL=https://hc-ping.com/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
#
# The runner pings this URL on every non-error tick (including scheduled
# skips) so healthchecks knows the LXC is up. If it doesn't hear from you
# within the expected period, IT will alert you - the case where the LXC is
# off / crashed and nothing local can send its own alert.
#
# See the "Self-hosted alternatives" note in README.md - Uptime Kuma is the
# common self-hosted replacement, uses the same push-URL model.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Git commit identity (used by the scheduled runner when it commits new
# publications to git). Optional - if unset, git uses its default identity.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# GIT_AUTHOR_NAME=Ofcom Amateur Callsign Mirror
# GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL=noreply@example.com

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Skip the git push step. Useful when running from a dev machine where you
# don't want to touch the real remote. When "true", commits happen locally
# but nothing is pushed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# SKIP_PUSH=true

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Debug logging - set to any non-empty value to get [DEBUG] lines through.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# DEBUG=true
